cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use MotifLine, please cite it as below, together with the methods and
  databases it relies on.
type: software
title: "MotifLine: a Snakemake workflow for motif discovery, hit calling and annotation from ChromBPNet and AlphaGenome attributions"
abstract: >-
  MotifLine computes DeepLIFT/SHAP attributions with ChromBPNet or AlphaGenome,
  discovers motifs with TF-MoDISco, calls motif instances with FiNeMo, and annotates
  the discovered patterns by TomTom comparison against HOCOMOCO H14 and JASPAR 2026.
  Both models share every stage after attribution.
authors:
  - family-names: Wang
    given-names: Qiankang
    alias: wangkant
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-27
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/wangkant/MotifLine"
keywords:
  - regulatory genomics
  - chromatin accessibility
  - transcription factor motifs
  - deep learning interpretation
  - ChromBPNet
  - AlphaGenome
  - TF-MoDISco
  - Snakemake
